spec:
  id: learning_order
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Curriculum
  compiler_stage: Learning Sequence
  description: >
purpose[5]: organize,sequence,prioritize,scaffold,engineering education.
philosophy[9]: Learning is cumulative.,New knowledge,builds upon,existing knowledge.,Concepts should appear,only after prerequisites,are mastered.,Practice strengthens,understanding.
pipeline[11]: Foundation,→,Core Concepts,→,Guided Practice,→,Independent Reasoning,→,Integration,→,Mastery
stages[8]: Awareness,Recognition,Understanding,Application,Analysis,Synthesis,Evaluation,Mastery
principles[7]: Concrete Before Abstract,Simple Before Complex,Local Before Global,Single Concept Before Combination,Theory Before Optimization,Reasoning Before Memorization,Fundamentals Before Frameworks
levels[6]: Beginner,Elementary,Intermediate,Advanced,Expert,Principal
foundation[6]: Variables,Data Types,Control Flow,Functions,Memory Basics,Basic Algorithms
core[6]: Data Structures,Algorithms,Software Design,Debugging,Testing,Version Control
advanced[6]: Operating Systems,Networking,Databases,Distributed Systems,Security,Compiler Design
expert[6]: Architecture,Performance Engineering,Reliability,AI Engineering,Autonomous Systems,Large Scale Systems
prerequisites[15]: Variables,→,Functions,Functions,→,Recursion,Arrays,→,Dynamic Programming,Threads,→,Concurrency,Networking,→,Distributed Systems
introduction[4]: Introduce One Major Idea,Reinforce Immediately,Connect To Prior Knowledge,Demonstrate With Examples
reinforcement[4]: Immediate Practice,Delayed Review,Cross Domain Application,Progressive Difficulty
mastery[5]: Explain,Implement,Debug,Optimize,Teach
transfer[4]: Same Domain,Similar Domain,Different Domain,Real Project
failure[4]: Detect Weak Concepts,Revisit Prerequisites,Generate Simpler Examples,Increase Practice
memory[4]: Track Learned Concepts,Track Weak Concepts,Track Mastered Skills,Track Forgotten Concepts
ekr:
  description: Every Engineering Knowledge Record
  stores[5]: Required Knowledge,Learning Stage,Difficulty,Prerequisites,Mastery Evidence
validation[8]: Every concept,has prerequisites.,Every lesson,has objectives.,Every objective,is measurable.,Learning order,is acyclic.
examples:
  Example_01:
    Learn: Arrays
    Before: Hash Tables
  Example_02:
    Learn: Processes
    Before: Containers
  Example_03:
    Learn: Synchronization
    Before: Distributed Consensus
  Example_04:
    Learn: Profiling
    Before: Performance Optimization
metrics[6]: Learning Velocity,Concept Retention,Prerequisite Coverage,Mastery Rate,Transfer Success,Curriculum Completeness
success[6]: Every learner,receives concepts,in an order that,"maximizes understanding,",retention and,engineering capability.
guarantees[5]: Structured Progression,Stable Foundations,Progressive Complexity,Knowledge Transfer,Engineering Readiness
future:
  adaptive_learning_paths: true
  personalized_curriculum: true
  graph_based_curriculum: true
  competency_tracking: true
  autonomous_curriculum_planning: true
